## FIRST · P1790 · original pre-run source and predictions

The [ACTUAL START](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1790#issuecomment-7158721509) is individually GET-verified. This freezes all fixture bytes and the oracle before any P1790 source is run. Both baseline compilers are the previously hashed, unchanged ordinary CLI at the exact adopted main 637653d917d1bc63acece382f0e014df3ae19e02 and the exact compare-only #1789 bcc0592fe95f4518c608f8e9dc54ca0090ee70ad.

**Caller need.** A receiver applies a mode to the active normal field and then to the standby reserve field of separate originally live records. With roles exchanged, the declared field positions reverse. The library API at the call sites is one byte exchange, with a typed write reference confined to one lexical loan and one byte input. The helper returns the displaced Copy. The other field and the original physical storage of each descriptor survive both calls. The two roots, four children, call invocations and two scopes must retain their own identities. The first loan is closed before the second call. The existing guard computes 4032 or 4096 bytes from 63 or 64 blocks. Selector outputs are 35 and 93. The caller deliberately chooses between propagating the freshly read mode and using a literal standby default of 19. No descriptor copy, heap, or failure protocol is added.

**Prediction.** Ordinary CHECK succeeds for the legal shapes below. Untouched C17 stops on the four mixed-position positives at V1-BACKEND-UNSUPPORTED. Static inspection finds an equal-index guard across the distinct originals. The existing publisher still has to prove each field and actual, each replay world, both loan exits and all six teardown places before a private remedy is justified. The same-index current and literal cases reach C17 and native on both pins. The displaced result same-index case reaches there on #1789 alone. On the planned main-based candidate it remains outside scope, as do mixed displaced result, sibling/pre-change reads as actuals, crossed observations and different-index reloan of the same original. These legal shapes are expected to retain CHECK0/C17 status 4. Lexical reference escape is expected to stop at CHECK3 with P8-EXIT-DEPENDENCY. Refusals leave named destination bytes and identity unchanged, a missing destination absent, and no staging file.

**Readout.** Oracle columns main, compare and candidate are expected C17 statuses. CHECK is common. Positions are zero-based in source declaration order, active followed by standby. Native tuples are planned bytes, selected byte, incoming byte, active old, active after, active sibling, standby old, standby after, standby sibling. Some tuples are C-only or compare-only until that NewLang pin emits. Check independently that the generated field addresses actually select the intended original and index as well as checking bytes. Exercise both rank branches and the direct-tail and named writer bodies. The archive rule is to preserve these exact inputs and original Gate0 separately from later observations.

**Well-factored C.** The frozen C library keeps guard, selection and exchange in a different translation unit from the caller. The driver parameterizes the same maintenance change, changing the declared target field role in one scope. Both physical variants use two automatic records, typed field addresses, fixed storage, two one-write calls, identical values/fallback, old Copies and ordinary teardown. C asserts original/field identity and sibling value preservation. Its pointer contract is live, writable u8 storage and synchronous nonretention, reflected by the NewLang lexical writer. Compare per-field, per-call and teardown evidence, alongside GCC/Clang native outcomes. Runtime policy and the cost of a wider audit are not inferred from an execution pass. Record the author and ordinary caller's UB-prevention dependency boundaries separately.

Frozen oracle is 1708 B, SHA-256 e1580f0964499faac086431716765b3aed3a9a28a741b9f441c55f919cdc6cac. Full input manifest SHA-256 c217ca08e05bd36a8e8bc7946fbc8ea430f29fb7093e75eb76dde3e4a808d511.

